//? Title: Integer-degree roots with Newton refinement
//? Subtitle: Actual power/ratio states, finite scaling and explicit initialization policies
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Approximate the principal nonnegative nth root with observable native Newton
updates. A hand-checkable cube-root step leads into the original known-root
checks and a50/n3 convergence diagnostic. Full-exponent and large-degree
controls explain the corrected initialization and arithmetic routes, while the
report distinguishes a small state change from a certified root error.
)

\toc

> Derive the update, then state its limits

For f(x)=xⁿ−a and positive x, Newton’s tangent update simplifies to
x_next=((n−1)x+a/x^(n−1))/n. For a>0 and fixed n, the principal root is simple;
sufficiently near it, the leading error is(n−1)e²/(2r), giving local quadratic
convergence until rounding dominates. Degree1 is the exact identity. Nonnegative
zero has a direct zero shortcut for degrees above one. This API deliberately
rejects negative radicands, including odd-degree cases, rather than silently
extending a different branch convention.

The implementation’s default stopping test compares consecutive states,
abs(next−before)<=10⁻¹⁵·abs(next), with at most100 updates. That is a numerical
termination rule, not a residual, correct-rounding or root-error certificate.
Trace metadata reports whether it passed; a deliberately exhausted budget
returns its finite current state with converged=false.

> One actual cube-root step for50

The original a=50,n=3 binary-exponent seed is4. Its actual power x² is16,
ratio50/16 is3.125 and next state(8+3.125)/3 is89/24. The first native record
supplies every value in the diagram. There is no report-side power/update
simulation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nth_root_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::nth_root_trace(50, 3);
    auto s = t.steps.front();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("seed", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual seed {}\nactual x squared {}", s.before, s.power));
    d.node("ratio", {7, 0},
           std::format("Actual50 / power\nratio {}", double(s.ratio)));
    d.node("next", {14, 0},
           std::format("Actual weighted update\nnext {:.10f}", s.after));
    d.edge("seed", "ratio").edge("ratio", "next");
    std::print("Actual first update: (2 * {} + {}) / 3 = {}.\n", s.before,
               double(s.ratio), s.after);
    d.save_svg("build/nth_root_tiny.svg");
}
```
