> Retain the fixed educational update budget honestly

The old diagnostic displayed states0 through7 and executed an additional final
assignment whose value was not plotted. The native fixed-budget study now
retains all eight actual assignments and all nine resulting states, with early
state-change acceptance disabled explicitly. Its table exposes stationary final
updates rather than extending an assumed quadratic rate past floating precision.
This experiment differs from the ordinary driver’s stopping policy.

The next figure displays actual states themselves. The complete errors against
native cbrt are printed, including the initial seed. Every value is captured
from the same canonical producer rather than a second handwritten Newton loop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nth_root_fixed.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::algorithms::nth_root_demo_study({8, 0, 1000});
    std::print("| actual state index | actual value | actual cbrt reference error |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.values.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, s.values[i], s.reference_errors[i]);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(s.indices, s.values, "actual fixed states", {124, 58, 237}).points(
        s.indices, s.values, "", {124, 58, 237}, 5).abline_h(s.reference,
                                                             {22, 163, 74}, 1).title("Original eight educational assignments, all states retained").x_label("actual completed updates").y_label("actual cube-root approximation").save_svg("build/nth_root_fixed.svg");
    std::print("\nActual assignments {}; state-change acceptance disabled; status {}.\n",
               s.trace.run.updates, s.trace.run.converged);
}
