> Finite extremes and large degrees need explicit arithmetic routes

For degrees through64, the corrected seed is2^ceil(e/n), where frexp gives
a=m·2^e. This binary upper seed avoids a huge first overshoot from a below-root
start and still gives4 for50/cube-root. The original finite-double
multiplication/update order is retained when safe. A
subnormal/nonpositive/nonfinite attempted power or nonfinite update selects a
checked long-double power/ratio fallback; actual attempted and fallback
multiplications are counted.

For degree above64, iterating n−1 multiplies per step would be unreasonable for
an int-sized n. That branch explicitly starts from exp(log(a)/n) in long double
and computes refinement ratios through exp(log(a)−(n−1)log(x)). It is an
initializer/refinement with transcendental functions, not a claim that all roots
are found solely by the elementary multiply/divide loop. The control table
identifies the route. Large-degree seeds are already close, so the actual update
count alone cannot measure their total computational cost.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nth_root_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    double tiny =
        std::numeric_limits<double>::denorm_min(), large =
        std::numeric_limits<double>::max();
    std::vector<std::pair<double, int>> pairs{{tiny, 2}, {large, 63},
                                              {large, 65},
                                              {tiny,
                                               std::numeric_limits<int>::max()},
                                              {0, 3}, {5, 1}};
    std::vector<std::string> names{"tiny/2", "max/63", "max/65", "tiny/intmax",
                                   "zero", "identity"};
    std::vector<double> updates;
    std::print("| control | actual result | log-derived seed | actual updates | actual power multiplies | " "widened updates | log-ratio updates | accepted/shortcut |\n| --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < pairs.size(); ++i) {
        auto[a, n] = pairs[i];
        auto r = dm::algorithms::nth_root_run(a, n);
        updates.push_back(r.updates);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", names[i],
                   r.value, r.log_seed, r.updates, r.power_multiplications,
                   r.widened_updates, r.log_ratio_updates, r.converged);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(updates, names, "actual assignments");
    p.title("Root scale/degree controls: actual assignments by route").x_label(
        "finite radicand / degree control").y_label("actual Newton updates; seed costs excluded").save_svg("build/nth_root_controls.svg");
}
```
